  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Working Group that advises on the transition of UNAIDS (facilitation of in-person meeting)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the UN80-initiative, UNAIDS is transitioning and integrating within the UN-system. Under the leadership of NL, as chair of the Bureau of the Programme Coordinating Board (PCB), a Working Group was established early 2026 to develop a plan for this transition. The Working Group (WG) is to present its final report with recommendations at the latest in October 2026, after which it will be discussed during a Special Session of the PCB on October 26th. To facilitate an in-depth discussion among WG-members on this complex matter, a physical meeting is held in Geneva on August 24-26. Since the budget for the work of the WG was approved after the UNAIDS budget was approved, additional funds have to be mobilized to cover the WG budget. The PCB has encouraged Member States to provide additional funding for this purpose. This physical meeting will be the first and only in-person meeting of the WG.</narrative>
  </description>
